From 6e022d8b89353b918339ac30ce0b1a28c6724666 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jky72 <jky72@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 09:50:36 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(input): handle IME composition so
 Korean/Japanese/Chinese can be typed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

par-term calls `set_ime_allowed(true)` but the event loop had no `WindowEvent::Ime` arm
at all, so composed text had no path to a PTY: the IME consumes the physical keys while
composing and par-term builds characters from physical keys, so typing Korean did
nothing - not even the physical letters arrived.

Add the missing handler:

* `Ime::Commit(text)` writes the text to the focused pane (or the tab terminal) the same
  way key input does. Not `paste_text`: that goes through `TerminalManager::paste`, which
  applies paste semantics (bracketed paste, newline handling) that typing must not have.
* `Ime::Preedit(text, cursor)` is kept in a new `ImeState` and drawn inline on the cursor
  cell, since composing text is not part of the grid and the child knows nothing about it
  until the commit.
* `set_ime_cursor_area` follows the composing caret so the candidate window stays put, and
  a modal egui UI keeps ownership of text input exactly as the key path does.

Verified with a real Korean IME: the log shows composed syllables arriving
(`commit "안" (0xC548)`, `commit "녕" (0xB155)`). Note that consonant-only runs such as
ㅎㅇㅎㅇ commit one jamo at a time (0x314E, 0x3147) - that is correct, not a bug, and
reading those as "composition is broken" is an easy mistake.

Also fix two lint failures that make the CI gate (`cargo clippy --all-targets
--all-features -- -D warnings`) fail:

* `par-term-input`: a doc list item ran into the next paragraph without a blank line
  (`clippy::doc_lazy_continuation`).
* `src/platform/notify.rs`: `ClickChannel::sender` is unread on Windows because every
  definition of `click_sender()` is Unix/macOS-only. Allow it there rather than leave the
  Windows clippy gate red.
